                                  style: { "--framer-text-alignment": `justify` },
                                  children: `Before we commit to one specific idea, we tend to search for alternatives. We come up with one that plays with the video game camera, one with progress bars and time, and another with switching the player-controlled object. I find these ideas to be somewhat promising, but ultimately, it falls short in terms of its expectancy. One of the judges made it clear that they seek for games that break players' expectations constantly. Simply treating certain video game elements in a unique and "non-conventional" way does the job, but only during the first-time user experience.`,
